**Definition 6.3 (paid descriptor import with stable heads).** The native
channel stages sender, mailbox and receiver descriptors as the latest
three immutable port-37 fields, in that order, as RCA Definition 13.2
requires. No bank assignment/staging occurs inside its protected allocation,
copy, completion-record and printing segment. Immediately after ACK,
before any further staging, find the third-last of those fields by the
fixed backwards-F scan and import it into a word register by native
RD/bit-test/literal-cons assignment/MR and Reverse. Compiler helpers
touch 32–36 only, so head 37 survives each assignment. The record is
the sender's original placement descriptor, not a descriptor of its stage.
Verify its O/39, initialized/sealed flag and recorded kind before registry
commitment, comparing kind with the preserved published-result register
rather than expecting a new native descriptor field. No extra channel
payload or receiver token is needed for this
owner-local metadata read.

On a later Convert, find the completed entry by finite word scans. Serialize
its exact descriptor into a new binary staging field on 37 using the
Base/dry-count/real-copy/full-descriptor/F/seal schema. Native unary-field
copy and Seek use that actual measured base to position 39. Copy its
payload length to distinct scratch and verify the closed block's delimiter.
Then import the selected binary payload through its own F, with the same
RD/finite-bit-test/literal-cons/MR/Reverse loop. No word assignment touches
39, and it is not extended during this scan. Exact measured length and
wrapper/kind/binding checks precede use. The current reader is O with its
actual archive token; no represented old token is consulted as authority.

The source record's native position remains stable even while bank helpers
extend 36 or scratch. Staging its descriptor precedes the scan, and none
of those intervening helpers extends 37. This is a closed retained block,
not a live end scanner or an arbitrary external pointer.

